<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.10" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="18776-5" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Plan of care note"/>
    <title>Plan of Treatment</title>
    <text><list><item>Stop oxycodone and diphenhydramine, keep acetaminophen scheduled, and finish 35 days of enoxaparin; review every medicine against the AGS Beers Criteria at each visit. Guideline: Management of Hip Fractures in Older Adults Evidence-Based Clinical Practice Guideline (2021); American Geriatrics Society 2023 updated AGS Beers Criteria for potentially inappropriate medication use in older adults (2023); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, Alzheimer&apos;s disease and hip/pelvic fracture monographs (2026) [S]</item><item>Home physical and occupational therapy, a home safety assessment, and a CDC STEADI fall-risk check at every visit. Guideline: Management of Hip Fractures in Older Adults Evidence-Based Clinical Practice Guideline (2021); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, Alzheimer&apos;s disease and hip/pelvic fracture monographs (2026) [S]</item><item>Replete vitamin D, aim for 1,000 to 1,200 mg of calcium a day from food, then obtain DXA and give intravenous zoledronic acid at about three months once calcium and kidney function are checked. Guideline: The clinician&apos;s guide to prevention and treatment of osteoporosis (2022); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, Alzheimer&apos;s disease and hip/pelvic fracture monographs (2026) [S]</item><item>Monitor dementia on the CMID schedule: yearly MoCA, FAST stage, and ADL and IADL scores; neuropsychiatric screen and depression screen at follow-up. Guideline: Alzheimer&apos;s Association clinical practice guideline for the Diagnostic Evaluation, Testing, Counseling, and Disclosure of Suspected Alzheimer&apos;s Disease and Related Disorders (DETeCD-ADRD) (2024); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, Alzheimer&apos;s disease and hip/pelvic fracture monographs (2026) [S]</item><item>Support the caregiver: Zarit Burden Interview at the first and six-month visits, weekly respite, a home health aide, caregiver education, and Alzheimer&apos;s Association support services. Guideline: Alzheimer&apos;s Association clinical practice guideline for the Diagnostic Evaluation, Testing, Counseling, and Disclosure of Suspected Alzheimer&apos;s Disease and Related Disorders (DETeCD-ADRD) (2024); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, Alzheimer&apos;s disease and hip/pelvic fracture monographs (2026) [S]</item><item>Advance care planning with the patient and spouse: confirm the health care agent, discuss goals of care, and complete a POLST form; revisit at each change in stage. Guideline: Alzheimer&apos;s Association clinical practice guideline for the Diagnostic Evaluation, Testing, Counseling, and Disclosure of Suspected Alzheimer&apos;s Disease and Related Disorders (DETeCD-ADRD) (2024); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, Alzheimer&apos;s disease and hip/pelvic fracture monographs (2026) [S]</item></list></text>

  </section>
